msgid "       N_{c}\\propto\\bar{\\alpha}\\theta \\tilde{G}\\phi_0^{2/3}."
msgstr "       N_{c}\\propto\\bar{\\alpha}\\theta \\tilde{G}\\phi_0^{2/3}."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:372
msgid ""
"Fit of Equation :eq:`CPlamint` to data from :math:`Re\\approx 4,000` "
"experiments. Hollow points indicate data not used in fitting the model."
msgstr ""
"Ajuste de la ecuación :eq:`CPlamint` a datos de :math:`Re\\approx 4,000` "
"experimentos. Los puntos huecos indican datos no utilizados para ajustar el "
"modelo."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:374
msgid ""
"At the highest values, however, a marked decrease begins. For these graphs, "
"the model fits were done for all points where increasing performance was "
"seen, because the model does not currently include a mechanism for the "
"decreasing performance. The values for :math:`k` were determined by the "
"Levenberg-Marquardt algorithm, and the value for the model was 0.030. The "
":math:`R^2` value for the fit is 0.958 and the sum of squared errors is "
"0.228 (mean pC* error of 0.128)."
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, en los valores más altos comienza una disminución notable. Para"
" estos gráficos, los ajustes del modelo se realizaron para todos los puntos "
"donde se observó un aumento del rendimiento, porque el modelo actualmente no"
" incluye un mecanismo para la disminución del rendimiento. Los valores para "
":math:`k` fueron determinados por el algoritmo de Levenberg-Marquardt, y el "
"valor para el modelo fue 0,030. El valor :math:`R^2` para el ajuste es 0,958"
" y la suma de los errores cuadráticos es 0,228 (error medio pC* de 0,128)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:376
msgid ""
"From the values given previously, the ratio :math:`\\frac{\\bar "
"\\Lambda_0}{\\bar{\\eta}}` can be calculated for the experimental "
"conditions. Equation :eq:`Ld` can be used to compute (:math:`\\bar "
"\\Lambda_0`). For these experiments, :math:`\\bar{D}_P` is taken to be the "
"average diameter of kaolinite clay particles, found by :cite:`Floc_Model-"
"wei_coagulation_2015` and :cite:`Floc_Model-sun_characterization_2015` to be"
" 7 :math:`\\mu m`. The concentration can be converted from NTU to the "
"necessary mass/volume (mg/L) unit by using as a proportion the measurement "
"reported by :cite:`Floc_Model-wei_coagulation_2015` of 68 NTU for 100 mg/L "
"of kaolinite clay. Last, the density was assumed to be 2.65 g/:math:`cm^3` "
"for kaolinite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:378
msgid ""
"For flocculation in laminar flows, data were used from the work of :cite"
":`Floc_Model-swetland_flocculation-sedimentation_2014`. "
":numref:`figure_PennockFig5` shows Equation :eq:`CPlamint` fit to results "
"for a capture velocity of 0.12 mm/s at two hydraulic residence times, five "
"influent turbidity values and a range of coagulant doses. :cite:`Floc_Model-"
"swetland_flocculation-sedimentation_2014` showed that the projected x-axis "
"intercept of the linear region of the data (with a log-log slope of 1 "
"according to her plotting of the data) was proportional to the capture "
"velocity used for sedimentation. Correspondingly, :math:`k` is expected to "
"be a function of capture velocity."
msgstr ""
"Para la floculación en flujos laminares, se utilizaron datos del trabajo de "
":cite:`Floc_Model-swetland_flocculation-sedimentation_2014`. "
":numref:`figure_PennockFig5` muestra que la ecuación :eq:`CPlamint` ajustada"
" a los resultados para una velocidad de captura de 0,12 mm/s en dos tiempos "
"de residencia hidráulica, cinco valores de turbidez influyente y un rango de"
" dosis de coagulante. :cite:`Floc_Model-swetland_flocculation-"
"sedimentation_2014` mostró que la intersección proyectada en el eje x de la "
"región lineal de los datos (con una pendiente logarítmica de 1 según su "
"trazado de los datos) era proporcional a la velocidad de captura utilizada "
"para la sedimentación. Correspondientemente, se espera que :math:`k` sea "
"función de la velocidad de captura."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:387
msgid ""
"Fit of Equation :eq:`CPlamint` to laminar flocculation data from :cite"
":`Floc_Model-swetland_flocculation-sedimentation_2014`."
msgstr ""
"Ajuste de la ecuación :eq:`CPlamint` a los datos de floculación laminar de "
":cite:`Floc_Model-swetland_flocculation-sedimentation_2014`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:390
msgid ""
"Referring to :numref:`figure_PennockFig5`, Equation :eq:`CPlamint` fits the "
"data from :cite:`Floc_Model-swetland_flocculation-sedimentation_2014` well "
"with a :math:`k` value of 0.027. The resulting :math:`R^2` for this fit is "
"0.844. The sum-squared error is 5.03, giving an average pC* error of 0.034 "
"for the fit."
msgstr ""
"En referencia a :numref:`figure_PennockFig5`, la ecuación :eq:`CPlamint` "
"ajusta los datos de :cite:`Floc_Model-swetland_flocculation-"
"sedimentation_2014` pozo con un valor de :math:`k` de 0,027. El :math:`R^2` "
"resultante para este ajuste es 0,844. El error suma al cuadrado es 5,03, lo "
"que da un error medio pC* de 0,034 para el ajuste."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:393 ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:531
msgid "Discussion"
msgstr "Discusión"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:395
msgid ""
"The goodness of fit seen in :numref:`figure_PennockFig3` and "
":numref:`figure_PennockFig5` indicate that the model captures the important "
"mechanisms governing flocculation performance for a wide range of coagulant "
"doses in both laminar and turbulent hydraulic flocculation. One of the "
"challenges in fitting the data pertained to the assumption made for the "
"characteristic diameter of PACl precipitate clusters, :math:`\\bar{D}_C`. "
"This value has significant influence on the value of :math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}`,"
" which in turn influences the values of the composite parameter (Equation "
":eq:`Paramlam`)."
msgstr ""
"La calidad del ajuste observada en :numref:`figure_PennockFig3` y "
":numref:`figure_PennockFig5` indica que el modelo captura los mecanismos "
"importantes que rigen el rendimiento de floculación para un amplio rango de "
"dosis de coagulante tanto en floculación hidráulica laminar como turbulenta."
" Uno de los desafíos para ajustar los datos se refería a la suposición hecha"
" para el diámetro característico de los cúmulos de precipitados PACl, "
":math:`\\bar{D}_C`. Este valor tiene una influencia significativa en el "
"valor de :math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}`, lo que a su vez influye en los valores del "
"parámetro compuesto (Ecuación :eq:`Paramlam`)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:397
msgid ""
"It is known that PACl contains aluminum monomers and oligomers as well as "
":math:`\\mathrm{Al_{13}}` and :math:`\\mathrm{Al_{30}}` nanoclusters, with "
"the larger :math:`\\mathrm{Al_{30}}` nanoclusters having a diameter of 1 nm "
"and a length of 2 nm :cite:`Floc_Model-mertens_polyaluminum_2012`. It has "
"been found, however, that the components of PACl self-aggregate and go on to"
" form larger clusters :cite:`Floc_Model-swetland_influence_2013`. For these "
"experiments, the value of :math:`\\bar{D}_\\mathrm{C}` was chosen based on "
"sizing experiments performed by Garland (2017) with a Malvern Zetasizer "
"Nano-ZS to analyze a 138.5 mg/L (as Aluminum) solution of PACl."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:399
#, python-format
msgid ""
"A limitation of the model can be seen in the data in "
":numref:`figure_PennockFig3` at higher values of the composite parameters. "
"After increasing steadily for all of the preceding range of coagulant doses,"
" the performance began to decline after the dose of 10.9 mg/L as Aluminum. A"
" simple hypothesis for the decline in performance (which corresponds with an"
" effluent turbidity increase over the five data points from 2.7 NTU to 11.1 "
"NTU) is that an increase in free PACl nanoparticles made a significant "
"contribution to the effluent turbidity. As the PACl concentration increased,"
" the coverage of reactor and clay platelet surfaces by coagulant became more"
" complete and the free coagulant concentration also increased. With very "
"high coagulant doses like the ones used in the upper end of the experimental"
" range, it is possible that the formation of PACl self-aggregates was "
"favorable, increasing the turbidity of the suspension. Indeed, calculation "
"of the volume fraction for the 10.9 mg/L experimental PACl dose gives a "
"volume fraction value (for clay and coagulant combined) of "
":math:`6.1\\times10^{-4}`, while for the highest dose of 98 mg/L as Al, the "
"value was :math:`8.3\\times10^{-4}`, a 37\\% increase due solely to the "
"increased contribution of PACl precipitates."
msgstr ""
"Una limitación del modelo puede verse en los datos en "
":numref:`figure_PennockFig3` a valores más altos de los parámetros "
"compuestos. Tras aumentar de forma constante en todo el rango anterior de "
"dosis de coagulante, el rendimiento comenzó a disminuir tras la dosis de "
"10,9 mg/L como aluminio. Una hipótesis sencilla para la disminución del "
"rendimiento (que corresponde a un aumento de turbidez del efluente en los "
"cinco puntos de datos de 2,7 NTU a 11,1 NTU) es que un aumento en "
"nanopartículas de PACl libre contribuyó significativamente a la turbidez del"
" efluente. A medida que aumentaba la concentración de PACl, la cobertura de "
"las superficies plaquetarias del reactor y de arcilla por coagulante se "
"completaba y también aumentaba la concentración de coagulante libre. Con "
"dosis muy altas de coagulante como las utilizadas en el extremo superior del"
" rango experimental, es posible que la formación de autoagregados de PACl "
"fuera favorable, aumentando la turbidez de la suspensión. De hecho, el "
"cálculo de la fracción volumétrica para la dosis experimental de PACl de "
"10,9 mg/L da un valor de fracción volumétrica (para arcilla y coagulante "
"combinados) de :math:`6.1\\times10^{-4}`, mientras que para la dosis más "
"alta de 98 mg/L como Al, el valor fue :math:`8.3\\times10^{-4}`, un aumento "
"del 37% debido únicamente a la mayor contribución de los precipitados de "
"PACl."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:401
msgid ""
"Another possibility is that as :math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}` increases above 0.5, "
"the resulting flocs are increasingly formed by PACl-PACl bonds instead of by"
" PACl-kaolinite bonds. If the PACl-PACl bonds are weaker than PACl-kaolinite"
" bonds, it is possible that attachment efficiency decreases for high "
":math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}`. The weakness of PACl-PACl bonds compared with PACl-"
"kaolinite bonds is suggested by the relative charges of PACl and kaolinite. "
"While PACl precipitate surfaces are positively charged, the surfaces of "
"kaolinite are mostly negatively charged :cite:`Floc_Model-"
"wei_coagulation_2015`. Therefore, it follows that PACl precipitates will "
"likely have more affinity for kaolinite surfaces than for other PACl "
"precipitates. The :math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}` calculated for the peak performance"
" was 0.52, and so it is possible that performance decreased past this point "
"because the strength of bonds for experiments at higher doses were weaker."
msgstr ""
"Otra posibilidad es que, a medida que :math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}` aumenta por "
"encima de 0,5, los flóculos resultantes se forman cada vez más por enlaces "
"PACl-PACl en lugar de por enlaces PACl-caolinita. Si los enlaces PACl-PACl "
"son más débiles que los enlaces PACl-caolinita, es posible que la eficiencia"
" de unión disminuya para altos :math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}`. La debilidad de los "
"enlaces PACl-PACl en comparación con los enlaces PACl-caolinita se sugiere "
"por las cargas relativas de PACl y caolinita. Mientras que las superficies "
"de precipitado PACl tienen carga positiva, las superficies de caolinita "
"están mayormente cargadas negativamente :cite:`Floc_Model-"
"wei_coagulation_2015`. Por lo tanto, se deduce que los precipitados PACl "
"probablemente tengan mayor afinidad por superficies de caolinita que para "
"otros precipitados PACl. El :math:`\\bar{\\Gamma}` calculado para el "
"rendimiento máximo fue 0,52, por lo que es posible que el rendimiento "
"disminuyera más allá de ese punto porque la resistencia de los enlaces para "
"experimentos a dosis más altas era más débil."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:403
msgid ""
"Applying the AguaClara flocculation model to the design of a hydraulic "
"flocculator indeed gives reasonable results. Assuming that a flocculator is "
"expected to receive sufficiently high turbidities that the influent "
"concentration can be neglected, Equation :eq:`GtlamSim` can be used. In "
"order for it to treat to a settled effluent of 3 NTU (pre-filtration) with "
"sufficient PACl to achieve a surface area coverage fraction of 0.5, it would"
" need to have a :math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta` of 99,600. :cite:`Floc_Model-"
"davis_introduction_2008` give the range of  :math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta` values"
" pertinent to flocculation of high turbidities as between 36,000 and 96,000,"
" so this result is reasonable. This analysis does not account for removal of"
" particles in a floc filter that would enable use of a lower value of "
":math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta`."
msgstr ""
"Aplicar el modelo de floculación de AguaClara al diseño de un floculador "
"hidráulico da resultados razonables. Suponiendo que se espera que un "
"floculador reciba turbidez suficientemente alta como para que se pueda "
"descuidar la concentración influyente, se puede usar la Ecuación "
":eq:`GtlamSim` . Para que trate hasta un efluente sedimentado de 3 NTU "
"(prefiltración) con suficiente PACl para lograr una fracción de cobertura "
"superficial de 0,5, necesitaría un :math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta` de 99.600. "
":cite:`Floc_Model-davis_introduction_2008` dar el rango de valores de  "
":math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta` pertinentes a la floculación de turbidez elevada "
"entre 36.000 y 96.000, por lo que este resultado es razonable. Este análisis"
" no tiene en cuenta la eliminación de partículas en un filtro de flóculos "
"que permitiría el uso de un valor menor de :math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:405
msgid ""
"Regarding flocculator design, recommended values of :math:`\\tilde{G}` in "
"flocculation range from :math:`10\\:\\mathrm{\\frac{1}{s}}` to "
":math:`100\\:\\mathrm{\\frac{1}{s}}`, which correspond to "
":math:`\\bar{\\varepsilon}` values of about 0.1 to 10 mW/kg :cite"
":`Floc_Model-mcconnachie_design_2000`. However, there is evidence that "
"higher velocity gradients are advantageous, as found by :cite:`Floc_Model-"
"garland_revisiting_2016` as well as the work done in this study, which made "
"use of energy dissipation rates of about 22 mW/kg. For hydraulic "
"flocculators, at least, designers should consider using higher energy "
"dissipation rates than conventionally used, since they have a much lower "
"ratio of maximum to average energy dissipation rate, leading to less floc "
"breakup at high energy dissipation rates compared to mechanically mixed "
"flocculators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:407
msgid ""
"The assumption that nonsettleable particle removal is proportional to "
"primary particle removal appears to be supported by the goodness of fit "
"supplied by the AguaClara  flocculation model to the data (see "
":numref:`figure_PennockFig3`). This assumption is likely included in the "
"values of :math:`k` fit by the model. A mechanistic understanding of "
":math:`k` will require that the proportionality between nonsettleable and "
"primary particles be understood explicitly. It is possible that :math:`k` is"
" a function of rapid mix effectiveness, and since :math:`k` predicts "
":math:`pC^*`, it will also be dependent on :math:`\\bar v_c`. Future "
"experiments at varying :math:`\\bar v_c` are planned. Currently, "
":math:`\\bar{\\alpha}` is calculated assuming that coagulant nanoparticle "
"attachment to the primary particles was accomplished very early on in the "
"flocculator, but if colloid coating by coagulant nanoparticles is dependent "
"upon diffusion rather than exclusively on hydraulic shear, it will be a "
"function of time in addition to :math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta`, making "
"flocculation less effective at high flow rates. Additionally, the use of "
":math:`\\bar{\\varepsilon}` (or :math:`\\tilde{G}`) assumes a uniform energy"
" dissipation rate in the flocculator. Any spatial deviation in the "
"laboratory flocculator from a uniform energy dissipation rate would have had"
" an impact on the values of :math:`k` relative to their theoretical values, "
"which are dictated by the rate of conversion of primary particles to flocs."
msgstr ""
"La suposición de que la eliminación de partículas no asentables es "
"proporcional a la eliminación de partículas primarias parece estar "
"respaldada por la bondad del ajuste proporcionada por el modelo de "
"floculación de AguaClara a los datos (véase :numref:`figure_PennockFig3`). "
"Esta suposición probablemente esté incluida en los valores de :math:`k` "
"ajuste por el modelo. Una comprensión mecanicista de :math:`k` requerirá que"
" la proporcionalidad entre partículas no asentables y primarias se entienda "
"explícitamente. Es posible que :math:`k` sea función de la efectividad de "
"mezcla rápida , y dado que :math:`k` predice :math:`pC^*`, también dependerá"
" de :math:`\\bar v_c`. Se planifican futuros experimentos a diferentes "
":math:`\\bar v_c` . Actualmente, :math:`\\bar{\\alpha}` se calcula asumiendo"
" que la unión de nanopartículas de coagulante a las partículas primarias se "
"logró muy temprano en el floculador, pero si el recubrimiento coloide por "
"nanopartículas de coagulante depende de la difusión y no exclusivamente del "
"cizallamiento hidráulico, será función del tiempo además de "
":math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta`, haciendo que la floculación sea menos efectiva a "
"altas caudales. Además, el uso de :math:`\\bar{\\varepsilon}` (o "
":math:`\\tilde{G}`) asume una tasa uniforme de disipación de energía en el "
"floculador. Cualquier desviación espacial en el floculador de laboratorio "
"respecto a una tasa uniforme de disipación de energía habría tenido un "
"impacto en los valores de :math:`k` relativos a sus valores teóricos, que "
"están dictados por la velocidad de conversión de partículas primarias en "
"flóculos."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:410
msgid "Summaries"
msgstr "Resúmenes"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:412
msgid ""
"We developed a model that predicts hydraulic flocculator performance. "
"Regardless of whether the flow is laminar or turbulent, viscous forces "
"control the relative velocities between particles on a collision path, and "
"the performance equation is "
":math:`pC^*=\\frac{3}{2}\\log_{10}\\left[\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\frac{6}{\\pi}\\right)^{2/3}\\pi"
" k\\bar{\\alpha}\\tilde{G}\\theta\\phi_0^{2/3}+1\\right]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:414
msgid ""
"Model predictions were compared with data from :cite:`Floc_Model-"
"swetland_flocculation-sedimentation_2014`. To validate the first equation "
"and the second equation in turbulent flow, experiments were conducted in "
"turbulent flow for initial conditions of :math:`\\frac{\\bar "
"\\Lambda}{\\bar{\\eta}}<1`. It was found that the viscous equation was "
"slightly more suitable in these conditions. Until further work is done on "
"delineating the relative predominance of viscous and inertial forces over "
"the range of turbulent flocculation conditions, the authors recommend using "
"the AguaClara flocculation model. For design purposes, this model indicates "
"that flocculator design is more sensitive to the desired effluent "
"concentration of particles than the range of influent concentrations that "
"might be encountered. This study also supports the use of higher energy "
"dissipation rates (or velocity gradients) than conventionally recommended "
"for hydraulic flocculators. Further work is needed to characterize the "
"functional dependence of :math:`k` on capture velocity and energy "
"dissipation rate, as well as the relationship between the final "
"concentrations of primary and primary particles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:419
msgid "Geometric Explanation of the Effects of Humic Acid on Flocculation"
msgstr "Explicación geométrica de los efectos del ácido húmico en la floculación"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:420
msgid ""
"Dissolved organic matter (DOM) is ubiquitous in natural waters and has "
"considerable influence on drinking water treatment, since the presence of "
"DOM can create a need for increased coagulant doses in addition to being a "
"precursor of disinfection byproducts (DBPs). This work evaluated use of "
"polyaluminum chloride (PACl) as a coagulant for a synthetic water to "
"determine the effect of DOM on the settled effluent turbidity. The research "
"employed the hydraulic flocculation performance model previously discussed "
"and made additions to the model algorithm to incorporate the effects of "
"humic acid on flocculation of inorganic particulate matter. Data were "
"obtained using a laminar-flow tube flocculator and a lamellar tube settler. "
"Two adjustable model parameters were used to fit data, one related to the "
"capture velocity used for sedimentation, and one that estimated the average "
"size of dissolved humic acid molecules. The modified model that accounted "
"for the presence of humic acid was able to independently predict the "
"experimental results from 60 experiments at a different influent turbidity. "
"This section is based on *Observations and a Geometric Explanation of the "
"Effects of Humic Acid on Flocculation* published in Environmental "
"Engineering Science in 2019 (DOI#10.1089/ees.2018.0405), and the reader is "
"encouraged to consult this article for more details."
msgstr ""
"La materia orgánica disuelta (DOD) es ubicua en aguas naturales y tiene una "
"influencia considerable en el tratamiento de agua de beber, ya que la "
"presencia de DOM puede generar la necesidad de dosis de coagulante "
"aumentadas además de ser precursora de subproductos de desinfección (DBPs). "
"Este trabajo evaluó el uso de cloruro de polialuminio (PACl) como coagulante"
" para agua sintética para determinar el efecto del DOM sobre la turbidez del"
" efluente sedimentado. La investigación empleó el modelo de rendimiento de "
"floculación hidráulica mencionado anteriormente y añadió al algoritmo del "
"modelo para incorporar los efectos del ácido húmico en la floculación de "
"partículas inorgánicas. Los datos se obtuvieron utilizando un floculador de "
"tubo de flujo laminar y un sedimentador de tubo lamelar. Se utilizaron dos "
"parámetros ajustables del modelo para ajustar los datos, uno relacionado con"
" la velocidad de captura utilizada para la sedimentación y otro que estimaba"
" el tamaño medio de moléculas de ácido húmico disuelto. El modelo modificado"
" que tuvo en cuenta la presencia de ácido húmico pudo predecir de forma "
"independiente los resultados experimentales de 60 experimentos en una "
"turbidez influyente diferente. Esta sección se basa en *Observaciones y una "
"explicación geométrica de los efectos del ácido húmico en la floculación* "
"publicada en Environmental Engineering Science en 2019 "
"(DOI#10.1089/ees.2018.0405), y se anima al lector a consultar este artículo "
"para más detalles."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:423
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introducción"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:424
msgid ""
"Optimal flocculation conditions for turbidity or pathogen removal are not "
"always the same as those for DOM removal (Hua and Reckhow, 2008). Because of"
" the variable composition of DOM, the mechanisms of removal could be "
"different for different types of DOM in water (Sharp and Jarvis, 2006). "
"Jarvis and Jefferson (2007) state that the mechanisms through which DOM is "
"removed include a combination of charge neutralization, adsorption, "
"entrapment, and complexation with coagulant polycations into suspended "
"particulate aggregates. The hydrophobic fraction of DOM, which includes "
"humic acids, is generally removed in coagulation more effectively than the "
"hydrophilic fraction (Marhaba et al., 2003; Matilainen et al., 2010). For "
"the system considered in this research, the mechanisms of DOM (humic acid) "
"attachment to coagulant (PACl with 10.6% Al2O3 w/w and basicity, OH/Al, of "
"2.1), appear to be adsorption (Yan et al., 2008) or complexation (Lin et "
"al., 2014; Xiong et al., 2018)."
msgstr ""
"Las condiciones óptimas de floculación para la turbidez o la eliminación de "
"patógenos no siempre son las mismas que para la eliminación de DOM (Hua y "
"Reckhow, 2008). Debido a la composición variable de la DOM, los mecanismos "
"de eliminación pueden ser diferentes para distintos tipos de DOM en agua "
"(Sharp y Jarvis, 2006). Jarvis y Jefferson (2007) afirman que los mecanismos"
" mediante los cuales se elimina la DOM incluyen una combinación de "
"neutralización de carga, adsorción, atrapamiento y complexación con "
"policaciones coagulantes en agregados particulados suspendidos. La fracción "
"hidrofóbica de DOM, que incluye ácidos húmicos, generalmente se elimina en "
"coagulación de forma más eficaz que la fracción hidrofílica (Marhaba et al.,"
" 2003; Matilainen et al., 2010). Para el sistema considerado en esta "
"investigación, los mecanismos de unión del DOM (ácido húmico) al coagulante "
"(PACl con 10,6% de Al2O3 p/w y basicidad, OH/Al, de 2,1) parecen ser la "
"adsorción (Yan et al., 2008) o la complejación (Lin et al., 2014; Xiong et "
"al., 2018)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:426
msgid ""
"Prehydrolyzed polymer coagulants, such as polyaluminum chloride (PACl), have"
" several advantages over conventional coagulants, such as alum, but the "
"characteristics of the raw water (e.g., pH, alkalinity, and DOM content) "
"affect the performance of different coagulants. As a result, prehydrolyzed "
"coagulants do not consistently improve the removal efficiency of DOM (Hu et "
"al., 2006)."
msgstr ""
"Los coagulantes poliméricos prehidrolizados, como el cloruro de polialuminio"
" (PACl), tienen varias ventajas sobre los coagulantes convencionales, como "
"el alumbre, pero las características del agua cruda (por ejemplo, pH, "
"alcalinidad y contenido de DOM) afectan el rendimiento de diferentes "
"coagulantes. Como resultado, los coagulantes prehidrolizados no mejoran "
"consistentemente la eficiencia de eliminación del DOM (Hu et al., 2006)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:428
msgid ""
"The research described in this paper builds on the AguaClara hydraulic "
"flocculation model developed by Pennock et al. (2018) and adds detail to the"
" attachment efficiency coefficient describing geometric and probabilistic "
"interactions between clay, coagulant, DOM, and reactor walls. The synthetic "
"raw water used in experiments added one type of DOM, humic acid, to a "
"previously studied synthetic system (Swetland et al., 2014) with the "
"expectation that the resulting system would be sufficiently well-"
"characterized to develop a predictive model."
msgstr ""
"La investigación descrita en este artículo se basa en el modelo de "
"floculación hidráulica de AguaClara desarrollado por Pennock et al. (2018) y"
" añade detalles al coeficiente de eficiencia de la fijación que describe las"
" interacciones geométricas y probabilísticas entre arcilla, coagulante, DOV "
"y paredes del reactor. El agua cruda sintético utilizado en experimentos "
"añadió un tipo de DOM, ácido húmico, a un sistema sintético previamente "
"estudiado (Swetland et al., 2014) con la expectativa de que el sistema "
"resultante estuviera suficientemente bien caracterizado para desarrollar un "
"modelo predictivo."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:431
msgid "Model Formation"
msgstr "Formación del modelo"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:433
msgid ""
"In laminar-flow flocculators, the velocity of one floc relative to another "
"scales with the average separation distance between flocs (Swetland et al., "
"2014). The time between floc collisions is inversely proportional to both "
":math:`\\phi` and the relative velocity between flocs. Because the relative "
"velocity between flocs is proportional to separation distance, the time "
"between collisions is proportional to :math:`{\\phi }^{\\frac{1}{3}}`, since"
" the average separation distance, :math:`\\overline \\Lambda`, is given by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:435
msgid ""
"\\overline \\Lambda=d_{\\mathrm P}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6\\phi "
"}\\right)}^{\\frac{1}{3}}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:439
msgid ""
"The result is that, for laminar flow, the average time for primary particle "
"collisions scales with :math:`{\\phi }^{-\\frac{2}{3}}` (Weber-Shirk and "
"Lion 2010)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:441
msgid ""
"A laminar-flow hydraulic flocculator model was developed and validated based"
" on the above analysis in Pennock et al. (2018) with the form"
msgstr ""
"Se desarrolló y validó un modelo de floculador hidráulico de flujo laminar "
"basado en el análisis anterior en Pennock et al. (2018) con la forma"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:443
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{p}C^{*}=\\frac{3}{2}{{\\log}_{10} "
"\\left[\\frac{2}{3}{\\left(\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\right)}^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\pi "
"k\\overline{\\alpha }\\tilde{G}\\theta {\\phi }^{\\frac{2}{3}}_0+1\\right]\\"
" },"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:448
msgid ""
"where  :math:`k` is a fitting parameter dependent on the value of "
":math:`V_{\\mathrm c}` used for sedimentation, :math:`\\overline{\\alpha }` "
"is the mean fraction of collisions that are successful (i.e., result in "
"aggregation), and :math:`\\mathrm{p}C^*` is defined as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:450
msgid ""
"\\mathrm{p}C^*=-{\\log \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{Effluent\\ "
"Turbidity}}{\\mathrm{Influent\\ Turbidity}}\\right)\\ }."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:455
msgid ""
"Equation :eq:`eq_AguaClara_Flocculation_Model`, referred to as the AguaClara"
" flocculation model in Pennock et al. (2018), is a Lagrangian hydrodynamic "
"model that assumes that the aggregation of primary particles is rate-"
"limiting. It further assumes that these particles, on average, will collide "
"when the volume of fluid swept out as one particle approaches the other is "
"equal to the average volume occupied by a single particle in the suspension."
" The time for these collisions to occur increases as flocculation proceeds, "
"since the concentration of primary particles decreases in a way that is "
"assumed to be first order with respect to collisions. Thus, with each "
"successive collision, the average volume occupied by primary particles "
"increases, and it takes longer for the next collision to occur. In Equation "
":eq:`eq_AguaClara_Flocculation_Model`, performance is linearly proportional "
"to the logarithm of the effective collision potential, "
":math:`\\log(\\overline{\\alpha }\\tilde{G}\\theta {\\phi }^{2/3}_0)`."
msgstr ""
"La ecuación :eq:`eq_AguaClara_Flocculation_Model`, conocida como el modelo "
"de floculación de AguaClara en Pennock et al. (2018), es un modelo "
"hidrodinámico lagrangiano que asume que la agregación de partículas "
"primarias es limitante de velocidad. Además, asume que estas partículas, de "
"media, colisionarán cuando el volumen de fluido barrido a medida que una "
"partícula se acerca a la otra es igual al volumen medio ocupado por una sola"
" partícula en la suspensión. El tiempo para que estas colisiones ocurran "
"aumenta a medida que avanza la floculación, ya que la concentración de "
"partículas primarias disminuye de una manera que se asume de primer orden "
"respecto a las colisiones. Así, con cada colisión sucesiva, el volumen medio"
" ocupado por las partículas primarias aumenta y tarda más en producirse la "
"siguiente colisión. En la ecuación :eq:`eq_AguaClara_Flocculation_Model`, el"
" rendimiento es linealmente proporcional al logaritmo del potencial efectivo"
" de colisión, :math:`\\log(\\overline{\\alpha }\\tilde{G}\\theta {\\phi "
"}^{2/3}_0)`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:457
msgid ""
"This group of parameters is the same as the group first described by "
"Swetland et al. (2014), with the exception that they used the estimated "
"fractional coverage of the colloid surface by coagulant, "
":math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_{\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}}`, as a measure of "
"attachment efficiency instead of :math:`\\overline{\\alpha }`. Pennock et "
"al. (2018) recognized that surface coverage of both particles participating "
"in a collision matters, and introduced :math:`\\overline{\\alpha }` to "
"convert the geometric information contained in "
":math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_{\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}}` to a probability of a "
"successful collision. Using data gathered by Swetland et al. (2014), Pennock"
" et al. (2018) were able to predict the results of independent laminar "
"flocculation experiments with no adjustable parameters in the absence of "
"added DOM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:459
msgid ""
"Experimental results obtained with added humic acid made clear that the "
"attachment efficiency was adversely affected by the addition of humic acid."
"  Referencing adsorption measurements by Davis (1982), a minority (his study"
" found 20\\%) of added DOM would be adsorbed by kaolinite at the "
"experimental pH of 7.5. Thus, most humic acid macromolecules were available "
"to attach to the added coagulant nanoparticles. The following simplifying "
"assumptions were made to account for the presence of humic acids: 1) humic "
"acid macromolecules attach to coagulant nanoparticles to form "
"nanoaggregates, 2) nanoaggregates attach to clay and to the reactor walls, "
"and 3) the surfaces of precipitated coagulant nanoparticles promote "
"adhesion, while the surfaces of bound humic acids prevent adhesion."
msgstr ""
"Los resultados experimentales obtenidos con ácido húmico añadido dejaron "
"claro que la eficiencia de unión se veía afectada negativamente por la "
"adición de ácido húmico. Referenciando mediciones de adsorción de Davis "
"(1982), una minoría (su estudio encontró un 20%) de DOM añadido sería "
"adsorbida por caolinita al pH experimental de 7,5. Así, la mayoría de las "
"macromoléculas de ácido húmico estaban disponibles para adherirse a las "
"nanopartículas coagulantes añadidas. Se hicieron las siguientes suposiciones"
" simplificadoras para tener en cuenta la presencia de ácidos húmicos: 1) las"
" macromoléculas de ácido húmico se adhieren a nanopartículas coagulantes "
"para formar nanoagregados, 2) los nanoagregados se adhieren a la arcilla y a"
" las paredes del reactor, y 3) las superficies de las nanopartículas de "
"coagulante precipitadas promueven la adhesión, mientras que las superficies "
"de los ácidos húmicos unidos impiden la adhesión."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:461
msgid ""
"In this study, humic acid macromolecules and PACl nanoparticles were modeled"
" as spheres. Based on the size of coagulant nanoparticles and humic acid "
"macromolecules, their number concentrations, :math:`N_{\\mathrm HA}` and "
":math:`N_{\\mathrm PACl}` respectively, can be estimated by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:463
msgid ""
"N_{\\mathrm HA}=\\ \\frac{C_{\\mathrm HA}}{{\\rho }_{\\mathrm HA}\\frac{\\pi"
" }{6}{d_{\\mathrm HA}}^3}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:467
msgid "and"
msgstr "y"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:469
msgid ""
"N_{\\mathrm PACl}=\\ \\frac{C_{\\mathrm PACl}}{{\\rho }_{\\mathrm "
"PACl}\\frac{\\pi }{6}{d_{\\mathrm PACl}}^3},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:473
msgid ""
"where :math:`C_{\\mathrm PACl}` is the dose of coagulant in mg/L as Al; "
":math:`C_{\\mathrm HA}` is the concentration of humic acid in mg/L; "
":math:`{\\rho }_{\\mathrm PACl}` is the density of the coagulant (Swetland "
"et al. (2013) found :math:`1,138 \\frac{\\mathrm kg}{\\mathrm m^3}`); "
":math:`{\\rho }_{\\mathrm HA}` is the density of humic acid, "
":math:`1,520\\frac{\\mathrm kg}{\\mathrm m^3}` (Sigma-Aldrich, 2014); "
":math:`d_{\\mathrm HA}` is the diameter of humic acid macromolecules (an "
"adjustable model parameter); and :math:`d_{\\mathrm PACl}` is the diameter "
"of precipitated PACl coagulant nanoparticles, taken to be 90 nm as found by "
"Dr. Casey Garland (2017)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:475
msgid ""
"A key model assumption was that humic acid macromolecules cannot adhere to a"
" coagulant surface that is occupied by a humic acid macromolecule, since "
"humic acid macromolecules are assumed to not appreciably self-aggregate. Li "
"et al. (2018) observed that for humic acid adsorption onto "
":math:`\\mathrm{Al_2O_3}` surfaces, the macromolecules adsorbed in a "
"monolayer. The outcome of this assumption is that humic acid macromolecules "
"attach to an uncovered surface of coagulant and do not stack on top of one "
"another. The available surface area of the PACl nanoparticle was modeled as "
"the surface area of an equivalent sphere. The amount of that area that is "
"occupied by an attached humic acid macromolecule was estimated as the "
"projected area of a sphere with volume equivalent to a humic acid "
"macromolecule.  A new variable describing the coverage of coagulant "
"nanoparticle surface area by humic acid macromolecules,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:477
msgid ""
" {\\overline{\\Gamma}_\\mathrm{HA-PACl}}=\\frac{{{\\frac{\\pi "
"}{4}d}_\\mathrm{HA}}^2}{{{\\pi "
"d}_\\mathrm{PACl}}^2}\\frac{N_\\mathrm{HA}}{N_\\mathrm{PACl}},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:482
msgid ""
"was created to be incorporated into the model (within "
":math:`\\overline{\\alpha }`) to represent the fraction of the PACl "
"nanoparticle surface area that is covered by humic acid macromolecules."
msgstr ""
"fue creado para incorporarse al modelo (dentro de :math:`\\overline{\\alpha "
"}`) para representar la fracción del área superficial de la nanopartícula "
"PACl que cubren las macromoléculas de ácidos húmicos."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:484
msgid ""
"The first two steps in particle aggregation, where humic acid macromolecules"
" attach to coagulant nanoparticles and then the resulting nanoaggregates "
"attach to clay surfaces, were assumed to be rapid because diffusion is an "
"effective transport process for nanoparticles (Benjamin and Lawler, 2013). "
"Subsequent to rapid mix, the clay particles with attached nanoaggregates "
"undergo collisions during the flocculation process and the aggregation "
"process is governed by fluid shear (Pennock et al., 2018). The success of a "
"collision between clay particles is hypothesized to be dependent on the "
"properties of the contact surfaces at the initial point of contact."
msgstr ""
"Los dos primeros pasos en la agregación de partículas, donde las "
"macromoléculas de ácido húmico se adhieren a nanopartículas coagulantes y "
"luego los nanoagregados resultantes se adhieren a las superficies de "
"arcilla, se asumieron rápidos porque la difusión es un proceso eficaz de "
"transporte para nanopartículas (Benjamin y Lawler, 2013). Posteriormente a "
"mezcla rápida, las partículas de arcilla con nanoagregados adheridos sufren "
"colisiones durante el proceso de floculación y este proceso está gobernado "
"por cizalladura de fluidos (Pennock et al., 2018). Se hipotetiza que el "
"éxito de una colisión entre partículas de arcilla depende de las propiedades"
" de las superficies de contacto en el punto inicial de contacto."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:486
msgid ""
"The three types of surfaces (PACl, humic acid, clay) have 6 (3!) potential "
"interactions as illustrated in :numref:`figure_Du_Fig2`."
msgstr ""
"Los tres tipos de superficies (PACl, ácido húmico, arcilla) tienen 6 (¡3!) "
"interacciones potenciales, como se ilustra en :numref:`figure_Du_Fig2`."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:495
msgid "Experimental Apparatus"
msgstr "Aparato experimental"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:495
msgid "Modes of collision between particles during flocculation."
msgstr "Modos de colisión entre partículas durante la floculación."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:498
msgid ""
"Of these interactions considered in the model, the collisions that will "
"result in attachment are assumed to involve at least one PACl nanoparticle "
"surface (:numref:`figure_Du_Fig2` A, B, C). The attachment efficiency is "
"hypothesized to be the sum of probability of these three types of "
"collisions, formally expressed as"
msgstr ""
"De estas interacciones consideradas en el modelo, se asume que las "
"colisiones que resultarán en la unión involucran al menos una superficie de "
"nanopartículas PACl (:numref:`figure_Du_Fig2` A, B, C). Se hipotetiza que la"
" eficiencia de unión es la suma de la probabilidad de estos tres tipos de "
"colisiones, expresada formalmente como"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:500
msgid ""
"\\overline{\\alpha }\\ ={\\overline{\\alpha }}_\\mathrm{PACl-"
"Clay}+{\\overline{\\alpha }}_\\mathrm{PACl-PACl}+{\\overline{\\alpha "
"}}_\\mathrm{HA-PACl},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:504
msgid ""
"where the subscripts define the two surfaces that are interacting. The "
"overbars indicate that all of these represent mean probabilities for an "
"entire suspension rather than the probabilities for specific particles."
msgstr ""
"donde los subíndices definen las dos superficies que interactúan. Las barras"
" superiores indican que todas estas representan probabilidades medias para "
"toda una suspensión en lugar de las probabilidades para partículas "
"específicas."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:506
msgid ""
"The probability of a clay surface colliding with a PACl surface "
"(:numref:`figure_Du_Fig2` A) is equal to twice the probability that the "
"first surface is clay (:math:`1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}`) "
"and the second surface is the PACl surface of a PACl-HA nanoaggregate "
"(:math:`\\left(1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}\\right){\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}`), since either of "
"two colliding particles could provide the clay surface or the PACl surface,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:508
msgid ""
"{\\overline{\\alpha }}_\\mathrm{PACl-"
"Clay}=2\\left(1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-"
"Clay}\\right)\\left[\\left(1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}\\right){\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}\\right]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:512
msgid ""
"The probability of a collision between the PACl surfaces of two PACl-HA "
"nanoaggregates (:math:`\\left(1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}\\right){\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}`) "
"(:numref:`figure_Du_Fig2` B) is given by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:514
msgid ""
"{\\overline{\\alpha}}_\\mathrm{PACl-"
"PACl}={\\left[\\left(1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}\\right){\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}\\right]}^2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:518
msgid ""
"The probability of a collision between a PACl surface of a PACl-HA "
"nanoaggregate (:math:`\\left(1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}\\right){\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}`) and an HA surface "
"of a PACl-HA nanoaggregate (:math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}`) (:numref:`figure_Du_Fig2` "
"C), or vice versa, is given by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:520
msgid ""
"{\\overline{\\alpha }}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}=2\\left[{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-"
"Clay}\\left(1-{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}\\right)\\right]\\left[{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-"
"PACl}{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}\\right],"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:524
msgid ""
"where the factor of 2 accounts for the possibility that either colliding "
"particle could contribute either surface type."
msgstr ""
"donde el factor 2 explica la posibilidad de que cualquiera de las partículas"
" colisionantes pueda contribuir a cualquiera de los tipos de superficie."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:526
msgid ""
"The model accounting for the presence of humic acids is modified from the "
"Pennock et al. (2018) model by redefining the attachment efficiency, "
":math:`\\overline{\\alpha }`, using Eq. 14 to account for the presence of "
"humic acid."
msgstr ""
"El modelo que explica la presencia de ácidos húmicos se modifica a partir "
"del modelo de Pennock et al. (2018) redefiniendo la eficiencia de "
"anclajación, :math:`\\overline{\\alpha }`, usando la Ecuación 14 para tener "
"en cuenta la presencia de ácido húmico."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:528
msgid ""
"The physical properties of humic acid vary with composition. The diameter of"
" humic acid macromolecules is estimated to range from 4 nm to 110 nm "
"(\\\"{O}sterberg, 1993). Because of the variation in the size of humic acid "
"macromolecules, the characteristic diameter of the humic acid macromolecules"
" was used as a fitting parameter. Thus, there are two adjustable model "
"parameters, :math:`k`(Equation :eq:`eq_AguaClara_Flocculation_Model`,), "
"which accounts for the sedimentation capture velocity, and "
":math:`d_\\mathrm{HA}`, which accounts for coagulant precipitate surface "
"coverage by humic acid.  These parameters were fit to results from "
"observations taken with an influent turbidity of 50 NTU; the model was then "
"validated by independently predicting results from experiments with an "
"influent turbidity of 100 NTU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:533
msgid ""
"The solubility of humic acid is highly pH-dependent, and additional "
"experimental results are needed to test the applicability of the model "
"approach as a function of varying pH. The experimental conditions were "
"designed to keep the pH relatively constant, and the pH change in the "
"experiments was small (7.5 :math:`\\pm` 0.3)."
msgstr ""
"La solubilidad del ácido húmico depende en gran medida del pH, y se "
"necesitan resultados experimentales adicionales para probar la aplicabilidad"
" del enfoque modelo en función de la variación del pH. Las condiciones "
"experimentales fueron diseñadas para mantener el pH relativamente constante,"
" y el cambio de pH en los experimentos fue pequeño (7,5 :math:`\\pm` 0,3)."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:535
msgid ""
"The model considered flocculation in the presence of humic acid as a two-"
"step process. Firstly, humic acid macromolecules attached to precipitated "
"coagulant nanoparticles. Then, the partially-coated coagulant nanoaggregates"
" could bind to clay and reactor wall surfaces.  Humic acid and coagulant "
"nanoparticles were treated as spheres when estimating the attachment "
"efficiency based on surface coverage and probability. The diameter of "
"precipitated PACl nanoparticles was experimentally measured to be 90 nm "
"(Garland, 2017), and a humic acid macromolecule diameter of 75 nm best fit "
"the observations. Wall loss of coagulant precipitates with humic acid "
"nanoaggregates was considered while direct wall loss of humic acid "
"macromolecules was not considered."
msgstr ""
"El modelo consideró la floculación en presencia de ácido húmico como un "
"proceso de dos pasos. En primer lugar, las macromoléculas de ácido húmico se"
" unieron a nanopartículas de coagulante precipitadas. Luego, los "
"nanoagregados coagulantes parcialmente recubiertos podían unirse a la "
"arcilla y a las superficies de las paredes del reactor. El ácido húmico y "
"las nanopartículas de coagulante se trataron como esferas al estimar la "
"eficiencia de unión basada en la cobertura superficial y la probabilidad. El"
" diámetro de las nanopartículas de PACl precipitadas se midió "
"experimentalmente en 90 nm (Garland, 2017), y un diámetro de macromolécula "
"de ácido húmico de 75 nm se ajustaba mejor a las observaciones. Se consideró"
" la pérdida de pared de precipitados coagulantes con nanoagregados de ácido "
"húmico, mientras que no se consideró la pérdida directa de pared de "
"macromoléculas de ácido húmico."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:537
msgid ""
"The characteristic humic acid dimension, :math:`d_\\mathrm{HA}`, has a "
"physical meaning, with the fitted value, 75 nm, falling within the range "
"(4-110 nm) reported by \\\"{O}sterberg (1993), and the model fits are well "
"correlated to the observations. The predictive capability of the model was "
"verified by predicting results under different experimental conditions with "
"no additional adjustable parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:539
msgid ""
"The flocculation model without the effects of humic acid shows that "
":math:`\\mathrm{p}C^*` is directly proportional to the log of the effective "
"collision potential, :math:`\\log(\\overline{\\alpha }\\tilde{G}\\theta "
"{\\phi }^{\\frac{2}{3}})`, and this relationship is still present in the "
"model with a modified attachment efficiency, :math:`\\overline{\\alpha },` "
"based on clay surface coverage by coagulant nanoparticles as adjusted for "
"the presence of humic acids."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:541
msgid ""
"The form of the flocculation model equation sets the interactions between "
"raw water properties (:math:`{\\phi }_0`), influent particle surface area "
"(which contributes to :math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}`), "
"coagulant precipitate size and dose (which contributes to "
":math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{PACl-Clay}` and "
":math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-PACl}`) , humic acid molecule size "
"and concentration (which contribute to :math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm"
"{HA-PACl}`), flocculator design (:math:`\\tilde{G}\\theta`), and clarifier "
"design (:math:`k`). In a gravity-powered water treatment plant operating at "
"constant flow rate, the flocculator and clarifier parameters are constant. "
"An increase in concentration of humic acid causes an increase in "
":math:`{\\overline{\\Gamma}}_\\mathrm{HA-PACl}`, which decreases "
":math:`\\mathrm{p}C^*` but can be compensated for by increasing coagulant "
"dose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:543
msgid ""
"The effect of the humic acid is to tie up a proportional amount of "
"coagulant. The turbidity doesn't begin to decrease until after all of the "
"humic acid has coated the coagulant nanoparticles and thus it is finally "
"possible for coagulant nanoparticles to remain sticky and attach to the "
"inorganic particles (see :numref:`figure_floc_model_HA` `by Yingda Du, et "
"al., 2019 <https://www.liebertpub.com/doi/abs/10.1089/ees.2018.0405>`_)"
msgstr ""
"El efecto del ácido húmico es atar una cantidad proporcional de coagulante. "
"La turbidez no comienza a disminuir hasta que todo el ácido húmico ha "
"recubierto las nanopartículas coagulantes y, por tanto, finalmente es "
"posible que las nanopartículas coagulantes permanezcan pegajosas y se "
"adhieran a las partículas inorgánicas (véase :numref:`figure_floc_model_HA` "
"`de Yingda Du, et al., 2019 "
"<https://www.liebertpub.com/doi/abs/10.1089/ees.2018.0405>`_)"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:552 ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:564
msgid "Du floc_model_HA"
msgstr "Du floc_model_HA"

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:552 ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:564
msgid ""
"Flocculation performance as a function of coagulant dose and humic acid "
"concentration."
msgstr ""
"El rendimiento de la floculación depende de la concentración de dosis de "
"coagulante y ácido húmico."

#: ../../Flocculation/Floc_Model.rst:554
msgid ""
"The data shown in :numref:`figure_floc_model_HA` can also be plotted in a "
"dimensionless form to show that all of the data converges reasonably well on"
" a single model curve (see :numref:`figure_floc_model_NTU_and_HA`)."
msgstr ""
"Los datos mostrados en :numref:`figure_floc_model_HA` también pueden "
"graficarse en forma adimensional para mostrar que todos los datos convergen "
"razonablemente bien en una sola curva de modelo (véase "
":numref:`figure_floc_model_NTU_and_HA`)."

